    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into favorable park factors and high-leverage lineup positions to maximize our 5x5 output. The premier play of the day is **Josh Naylor** (78.46), who benefits from a prime matchup against Aaron Civale and a massive +10% park boost, anchoring our lineup from the #3 spot. **Corbin Carroll** (74.78) remains a central engine for our pursuit of stolen bases; despite a marginal penalty for Landen Roupp\u2019s quick pop-time, his +8% boost from batting second and a strong xwOBA profile keep his ceiling near elite levels. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.28) and **James Wood** (66.50) project as high-efficiency starters; **Tyler Soderstrom** specifically capitalizes on a high-upside combination of a +10% park factor and a clean +4% boost from hitting cleanup against Luis Castillo.\n\nWhile our starters are locked in, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (65.22) and **Brice Turang** (61.69) provide strong utility value by exploiting favorable platoon splits and high-order positioning. **Jose Caballero** remains our most volatile piece at a 51.84 score; while he is a key speed asset, his score is suppressed today by a -13% platoon penalty and an elite hold from the opposing battery. The most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Carson Williams** (37.91). While his park environment was excellent, the negative impact of facing a tough arm in Kyle Bradish\u2014combined with the projected #9 batting spot\u2014dropped him well below our start threshold compared to the more stable volume offered by **Cole Young** (56.89) or **Travis Bazzana** (57.55).\n\nAll starters are currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status, which introduces minor variance risk if managers shift the batting order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Seiya Suzuki** (49.63) and **Henry Bolte** (49.02), both of whom are hovering near our bench floor; should late-breaking news confirm they are pushed lower in their respective lineups, they may be subject to early substitution to preserve our total game caps. With **Mickey Moniak** and **Austin Riley** currently unavailable, we are relying on our depth to carry the load, and we will monitor weather updates for any wind shifts that might dampen the projected output for our power-heavy outfielders.",
